{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** The Fibonacci numbers start `F(0) = 0`, `F(1) = 1`, and each one after is the sum of the two before it: `F(n) = F(n − 1) + F(n − 2)`. Given `n`, return `F(n)`."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/751e9912-83c3-4d39-86a3-75ef8a408472.svg",
      "alt": "The Fibonacci numbers from F(0) to F(7): 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13. Each is the sum of the two before it, so F(7) = 5 + 8 = 13. To compute them in order you only ever need the last two.",
      "width": 826,
      "height": 357,
